From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: hand a firmware crash found on resume to crash
 recovery

With WoWLAN the firmware keeps running while the system sleeps, and it
can crash then. ath11k_mhi_resume() forces the MHI resume regardless of
the device state, but a crashed device is in RDDM and doesn't return to
M0. The resume fails after the timeout:

  mhi mhi0: Resuming from non M3 state (SYS ERROR)
  ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: failed to resume mhi: -5

mac80211 then reports that the hardware became unavailable and stops
the device. The reset that follows can't connect to the firmware
either, Wi-Fi stays off, and every later resume waits about 20 seconds
in ath11k until the next cold boot.

Check for RDDM and SYS_ERR before forcing the resume. If the firmware
crashed, schedule a reset, fail the MHI resume, and report the WoW
resume as done while the crash is pending, as when the firmware crashes
during the suspend: the reset at PM_POST_SUSPEND then restarts the
device like after any other crash.

Tested-on: WCN6855 hw2.1 PCI WLAN.HSP.1.1-03125-QCAHSPSWPL_V1_V2_SILICONZ_LITE-3.6510.41

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c |  7 +++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c  | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index 1a22d9cd2..1cf3ac8f5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -1361,6 +1361,13 @@ static int ath11k_core_resume_wow(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 
 	ret = ath11k_hif_resume(ab);
 	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * The firmware crashed while the system was asleep. Resume
+		 * as if WoW had worked; the restart follows the resume.
+		 */
+		if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_PENDING, &ab->dev_flags))
+			return 0;
+
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to resume hif during resume: %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c
index a12382e55..58109aa28 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c
@@ -489,6 +489,19 @@ int ath11k_mhi_resume(struct ath11k_pci *ab_pci)
 	struct ath11k_base *ab = ab_pci->ab;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * If the firmware crashed while the system was asleep, the device
+	 * is in RDDM and won't return to M0: a forced resume would only wait
+	 * for the timeout. Hand it to crash recovery, which restarts it once
+	 * the system is up.
+	 */
+	if (mhi_get_exec_env(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl) == MHI_EE_RDDM ||
+	    mhi_get_mhi_state(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl) == MHI_STATE_SYS_ERR) {
+		ath11k_warn(ab, "firmware crashed during suspend\n");
+		ath11k_core_schedule_reset(ab);
+		return -ESHUTDOWN;
+	}
+
 	/* Do force MHI resume as some devices like QCA6390, WCN6855
 	 * are not in M3 state but they are functional. So just ignore
 	 * the MHI state while resuming.
